  "note": "Hand-authored cut for the slender proportion. Coordinates are master pixels on the 512x512 canvas. Slender is 6.5 heads to standard's 4, so nothing here is a scaled copy of the standard cut: the head is ~68px instead of ~110, the neck is actually visible rather than a seam-filler, the torso runs long under a full-length skirt, and the tail hangs beside the hip rather than behind the waist. Shapes are generous where a colour gate can make the precise cut (the hairline: bangs are saturated blue, the forehead under them is skin) and tight where none can, because the navy dress and the navy hair share a palette. Grow is 1px rather than standard's 2: slender is the same 445px tall but 6.5 heads instead of 4, so its outlines and limbs are proportionally much finer and a 2px grow pushed every part a visible step over its neighbour. The sleeve polygons stop at x=198 rather than 206: the white apron and bodice begin there, and a wider arm claimed them, which alone was half the rest-recomposite error.",
